Setting Up Secure Shell Access:-
==============================

ssh-keygen -t ed25519

ssh-copy-id -p port_name hostname@ip_address 

Adding configuration :- sudo vim ~/.ssh/config 

ls ~/.ssh --> To see the ssh-key token's .pub 

Configure the firewall:-
======================

Using `UFW` on all three ubuntu servers

Note:-"" The goal is to secure the servers while allowing the traffic required for SSH and later, K3s""

Allow SSH before enable UFW:- 

--> sudo ufw allow 22/tcp 

--> sudo ufw allow from 192.168.1.0/24

sudo ufw enable

sudo ufw status

After configuration of firewall (verification process):-
======================================================

From cluster-master
===================

ssh cluster-worker1

ssh cluster-worker2

From cluster-worker1
====================

ping -c 3 cluster-master

From cluster-worker2
====================

ping -c 3 cluster-master 


Time Synchronization
====================

timedatectl status 

O/p:-

"""
	System clock synchronized: yes
	NTP services: active
""" 

sudo timedatectl set-ntp ture --> It the sychronized is not active

Note:-
=====
"""
	The times should be essentially identical on all the server / cluster (i.e cluster-master,cluster-worker1,cluster-worker2)
"""

Verification after Time Synchronization:-
=======================================

date --> It should be same on all the cluster-worker1,2 

